      "id": "ea7a6078b27f-q8",
      "number": 8,
      "question": "Baisakhi Festival is majorly celebrated in the states of _______ and ________.",
      "questionHtml": "Baisakhi Festival is majorly celebrated in the states of _______ and ________.",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "Nagaland, Tripura",
          "html": "Nagaland, Tripura&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "Rajasthan, Madhya Pradesh",
          "html": "Rajasthan, Madhya Pradesh&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "Punjab, Haryana",
          "html": "Punjab, Haryana&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "Tamil Nadu, Kerala",
          "html": "Tamil Nadu, Kerala&nbsp;&nbsp;"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "C",
      "solution": "<p>The correct answer is <span style=\"color: (33, 37, 41);\"><u><strong>Punjab, Haryana</strong></u>.</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;\"><img height=\"26px\" src=\"//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/key-point-image.png\" width=\"26px\" /><strong><span style=\"vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;\"><u>Key Points</u></span></strong></span></p>\n\n<ul style=\"color: (33, 37, 41); user-select: auto;\">\n\t<li style=\"user-select: auto;\"><span style=\"font-weight: bolder; user-select: auto;\">Baisakhi </span>is a famous festival of <span style=\"font-weight: bolder; user-select: auto;\">Punjab</span>.</li>\n\t<li style=\"user-select: auto;\"><span style=\"color: (32, 33, 36); user-select: auto;\">The festival <span style=\"font-weight: bolder; user-select: auto;\">Baisakhi</span> is celebrated to mark the <span style=\"font-weight: bolder; user-select: auto;\">spring in India. </span></span></li>\n\t<li style=\"user-select: auto;\"><span style=\"color: (32, 33, 36); user-select: auto;\">This festival is known also as <span style=\"font-weight: bolder; user-select: auto;\">Sikh new year </span>and Sikhs pay tribute to their tenth guru, <span style=\"font-weight: bolder; user-select: auto;\">Guru Gobind Singh</span>.</span></li>\n\t<li style=\"user-select: auto;\"><span style=\"font-weight: bolder; user-select: auto;\">Vaisakhi Sankranti</span><span style=\"color: (32, 33, 36); user-select: auto;\"> is celebrated on the first day of Vaisakha, This day is also known as Sattuā or Satwahi.<span style=\"color: (32, 33, 36); user-select: auto;\">​</span></span></li>\n</ul>\n\n<p style=\"user-select: auto;\"><span style=\"color: (32, 33, 36); user-select: auto;\"><span style=\"display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;\"><img height=\"26px\" src=\"//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/additional-information-image.png\" width=\"26px\" /><strong><span style=\"vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;\"><u>Additional Information</u></span></strong></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"user-select: auto;\"><span style=\"color: (32, 33, 36); user-select: auto;\"><span style=\"font-weight: bolder; user-select: auto;\"><u style=\"user-select: auto;\">Some Important Festival Of India:</u></span></span></p>\n\n<ul style=\"color: (33, 37, 41);\">\n\t<li style=\"user-select: auto;\"><span style=\"color: (32, 33, 36); user-select: auto;\">​</span><span style=\"color: (51, 51, 51);\">Andhra Pradesh- Dasara, Ugadi, Deccan Festival, Brahmotsavam.</span></li>\n\t<li style=\"user-select: auto;\"><span style=\"color: (51, 51, 51);\">Assam- Ambubachi, Bhogali Bihu, Baishagu, Dehing Patkai.</span></li>\n\t<li style=\"user-select: auto;\"><span style=\"color: (51, 51, 51);\">Chhattisgarh- Maghi Purnima, Bastar Dussehra.</span></li>\n\t<li style=\"user-select: auto;\"><span style=\"color: (51, 51, 51);\">Goa- Sunburn festival, Ladain, Mando.</span></li>\n\t<li style=\"user-select: auto;\"><span style=\"color: (51, 51, 51);\">Gujarat- Navratri, Janmashtami, Kutch Utsav, Uttarayana.</span></li>\n</ul>\n",
